## Extra packages for the headless Kali Live image.
## Required by the project specification:
## Sane Kali baseline (the minimal variant ships no metapackage at all;
## under 'default' this is already satisfied by kali-linux-default)
kali-linux-core
openssh-server
network-manager
wpasupplicant
wireless-regdb

## Radio firmware, EXPLICIT (2026-10-28, owner direction: no firmware diet —
## inclusion by default). These arrived only transitively via upstream's
## pinned lists before, so an upstream list change could silently strip them
## (the #51 Legion incident: iwlwifi failed with error -1010 + hci0 could not
## read supported features — root cause there was a Windows-fast-startup
## wedged combo card, but the image must never be the variable).
## iwlwifi covers ALL Intel wireless generations (212 ucode files in #44);
## ibt-* Intel Bluetooth blobs ship in the firmware-iwlwifi tree.
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-linux-nonfree
firmware-misc-nonfree
firmware-atheros
firmware-brcm80211
firmware-realtek
bluez-firmware
iw
iproute2
avahi-daemon
## mDNS client NSS module: <name>.local resolution is how the boot-time
## duplicate-hostname probe sees other machines (avahi-daemon only recommends it)
libnss-mdns
curl
git
tmux
tcpdump
## WireGuard access channel (M1): the tunnel identity itself is generated on
## first boot and persisted to the KLHCONFIG partition — nothing baked, see
## README "WireGuard access".
wireguard-tools
dislocker
systemd-timesyncd
